---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About the collection — nnxyz">
  <article class="text-page">
    <h1>About the collection</h1>
    <p class="collector-introduction">
      My eye kept returning to these works. I found myself looking for patterns,
      and for the feeling in each image. Some seemed joyous; others felt angry.
      That range kept me looking.
    </p>
    <p>
      I found a similar visual character and range in scrimshaw’s work. I
      remember both artists publishing on Nifty Ink during the same period.
    </p>
    <p class="small-note">
      Collector introduction, edited from the collector’s account.
    </p>
    <h2>The artwork and the archive</h2>
    <p>
      This gallery brings together 600 nnxyz works and 26 works by scrimshaw.
      The Nifty Ink archive preserves 574 drawings representing 633 owned
      editions at its saved snapshots. Another 52 Abstract works have been
      recovered from the collector’s earlier public gallery.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each Nifty Ink drawing is reconstructed as a native vector image from its
      archived brush paths. You can enlarge it, download its SVG, or watch the
      drawing emerge. The paths and their order are recorded; playback timing is
      reconstructed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Abstract is presented from its original published JPEGs, with enlargement
      and downloads. Its earlier gallery records fifty numbered pieces, an
      origin titled #0000 and a proof-of-stake work titled #pos. The recovered
      records do not include brush paths or establish current token ownership.
    </p>
    <p>
      The artwork pages link to the collected NFTs. Nifty Ink links use the
      editions recorded in the archived collection; Abstract links come from the
      collector’s earlier gallery.
    </p>
    <h2>Collection history</h2>
    <p>
      NNOTB means “New Nifty on the Block,” as recorded in the collector’s
      <a href="https://www.thingelstad.com/art/nnxyz/">earlier gallery</a>. That
      account describes Faces as the first Nifty Ink series and Rawblocks as the
      third. Each collection keeps its original artwork titles; an “origin”
      title does not necessarily mark the first recorded drawing.
    </p>
    <p>
      The earlier{' '}
      <a href="https://www.thingelstad.com/art/nnxyz/abstract/">
        Abstract account
      </a>
      also lists scrimshaw.eth as the gift recipient beside #06. This is
      historical context from the collector’s account, separate from the
      galleries’ visual comparisons.
    </p>
    <h2>Curated with AI</h2>
    <p>
      The gallery texts start with the artwork and archived records.
      They offer specific ways of looking, rather than claims about what the
      artist intended. Technical facts, collection position and interpretations
      are kept distinct.
    </p>
    <p>
      The gallery shows an owned subset. Title sequence does not establish
      creation order or a complete catalogue of either artist’s work. Related
      works are visual comparisons, not evidence of influence.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/#collections">Explore the collection galleries →</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/">Return to the collection →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
